<BaseLayout
  title="Super Mario Odyssey — Is It Still the Best 3D Mario?"
  description="A buying guide for Super Mario Odyssey on Switch: sandbox kingdoms, capture mechanic, and where to buy it cheapest in 2026."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Super Mario Odyssey — Is It Still the Best 3D Mario?</h1>
    <p class="meta">Nintendo Switch · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Super Mario Odyssey</strong> is the globe-trotting 3D platformer that
      pairs Mario with Cappy, a hat that lets you "capture" and control enemies and
      objects. Years on, many still call it the best 3D Mario ever made.
    </p>

    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Dozens of sandbox "kingdoms" built for exploration and replay</li>
      <li>The capture mechanic — possess a T-Rex, a bullet bill, a taxi</li>
      <li>Collectathon depth: 800+ moon collectibles for completionists</li>
      <li>Two-player co-op (one drives Mario, one drives Cappy)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why it's often discounted</h2>
    <p>
      Unlike brand-new releases, Odyssey is a mature title that regularly appears in
      Nintendo's budget "Selects" range and seasonal eShop sales. It's one of the
      easier first-party games to find under MSRP.
    </p>

    <h2>Digital vs physical</h2>
    <p>
      Same rule as always: digital for instant access, physical if you want to trade
      it in. The install is moderate, so storage isn't a deciding factor.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to buy cheapest</h2>
    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Super+Mario+Odyssey+Switch"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

